  "intended_text": "Bananas are a yellow fruit that are rich in potassium, calcium and other minerals and vitamins. When they are raw bananas are green in color, but when they become ripe they turn yellow, and when they start to rot they turn brown in color. They are very sweet and are extremely fibrous. Fun fact about bananas is that even though they don't look like a tree, it's actually not a tree, it's a plant. Banana leaves are used for eating as plates in South India."
